'''Lance Jacob Strulovitch''' ({{IPAc-en|ˈ|l|ɑː|n|s|_|ˌ|s|t|r|əl|ə|v|ɪ|tʃ}}; born 29 October 1998), commonly known as '''Lance Stroll''' ({{IPAc-en|ˌ|s|t|r|oʊ|l}}), is a Canadian [[racing driver]] who competes in [[Formula One]] for [[Aston Martin in Formula One|Aston Martin]].

Born and raised in [[Montreal]], Stroll is the son of billionaire businessman [[Lawrence Stroll]], owner of the Aston Martin F1 Team, and his Belgian ex-wife. Stroll began competitive [[kart racing]] aged 10, winning several regional and national titles. A member of the [[Ferrari Driver Academy]] since 2010, Stroll graduated to [[junior formulae]] in 2014, winning his first title at the [[2014 Italian F4 Championship|Italian F4 Championship]] that year with [[Prema Racing|Prema]]. He then won the [[Toyota Racing Series]] in [[2015 Toyota Racing Series|2015]] with [[M2 Competition|M2]], and dominated the [[FIA Formula 3 European Championship]] in {{FIAF3|2016}} with Prema.

Following his record-breaking successes in [[Formula Three]],{{efn|Including most wins in a season (14), most fastest laps in a season (13, shared with [[Felix Rosenqvist]]), and largest championship-winning margin (187), all in the [[2016 FIA Formula 3 European Championship]].}} Stroll signed for [[Williams Racing|Williams]] in {{F1|2017}} to partner [[Felipe Massa]], making his Formula One debut at the {{F1GP|2017|Australian}}, aged 18. He scored his maiden podium finish in [[2017 Azerbaijan Grand Prix|Azerbaijan]] that year, becoming the [[List of Formula One driver records#Youngest drivers to score a podium finish|second-youngest driver to score a podium]]. Stroll finished a season-best eighth at the [[2018 Azerbaijan Grand Prix|same Grand Prix]] in {{F1|2018}}, driving the [[Williams FW41|FW41]]. After two seasons at Williams, Stroll signed for [[Racing Point]]—which had recently been [[Pay driver|acquired by his father]]—in {{F1|2019}} to partner [[Sergio Pérez]], finishing fourth at the rain-affected {{F1GP|2019|German}}. In {{F1|2020}}, Stroll achieved his maiden [[List of Formula One polesitters|pole position]] at the {{F1GP|2020|Turkish}}, with podiums at the [[2020 Italian Grand Prix|Italian]] and [[2020 Sakhir Grand Prix|Sakhir]] Grands Prix. Stroll remained at the re-branded [[Aston Martin in Formula One|Aston Martin]] in {{F1|2021}}, partnered by [[Sebastian Vettel]] for two seasons. Stroll has been teammates with [[Fernando Alonso]] since {{F1|2023}}, finishing a career-best tenth in the [[World Drivers' Championship]] that year.

As of the {{Latest F1GP}}, Stroll has achieved {{Numbertoword|{{F1stat|STR|poles}}}} pole position and {{Numbertoword|{{F1stat|STR|podiums}}}} podiums in Formula One. Stroll is contracted to remain at Aston Martin until at least the end of the 2026 season. Outside of Formula One, Stroll competed in two editions of the [[24 Hours of Daytona]] in [[2016 24 Hours of Daytona|2016]] and [[2018 24 Hours of Daytona|2018]] with [[Chip Ganassi Racing|CGR]] and [[Jackie Chan DC Racing|Jackie Chan DC]], respectively.

==Early and personal life==
Lance Strulovitch was born on 29 October 1998 in [[Montreal]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport-total.com/formel-1/news/sergio-perez-ich-wuerde-meinen-sohn-nicht-rausschmeissen-20081106 |title=Sergio Perez: 'Ich würde meinen Sohn nicht rausschmeißen' |language=de |work=Motorsport Total |first=Christian |last=Nimmervoll |date=11 August 2020 |access-date=4 July 2021 |archive-date=11 July 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210711052659/https://www.motorsport-total.com/formel-1/news/sergio-perez-ich-wuerde-meinen-sohn-nicht-rausschmeissen-20081106 |url-status=live }}</ref> Stroll is the son of Canadian billionaire businessman [[Lawrence Stroll]]—part-owner and executive chairman of [[Aston Martin]], as well as owner of [[Aston Martin in Formula One|its Formula One team]]—and Belgian fashion designer Claire-Anne Stroll ({{nee}} Callens), and has an older sister named [[Chloe Stroll|Chloe]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.dhnet.be/sports/f1/f1-la-maman-de-lance-stroll-est-belge-58220c0acd70fb896a66d27c|title=F1: La maman de Lance Stroll est Belge!|language=fr|trans-title=Lance Stroll's mother is Belgian!|date=8 November 2016|work=DH.be|access-date=30 March 2017|archive-date=29 August 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170829032850/http://www.dhnet.be/sports/f1/f1-la-maman-de-lance-stroll-est-belge-58220c0acd70fb896a66d27c|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.jwire.com.au/jewish-canadian-to-compete-in-melbournes-formula-one/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170424233405/http://www.jwire.com.au/jewish-canadian-to-compete-in-melbournes-formula-one/|url-status=dead|title=Jewish Canadian to compete in Melbourne's Formula One.|date=15 March 2017|archive-date=24 April 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.jewishnews.net.au/jewish-driver-set-f1-debut/60565|title=Jewish driver set for F1 debut – The Australian Jewish News|date=23 March 2017|website=jewishnews.net.au|access-date=20 May 2017|archive-date=23 April 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170423081923/https://www.jewishnews.net.au/jewish-driver-set-f1-debut/60565|url-status=live}}</ref> His parents are divorced and his father has since remarried to Raquel Diniz.<ref>{{Cite web |date=14 July 2021 |title=Whatever it takes – Lawrence Stroll determined to lead Aston Martin to F1 glory |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/lawrence-stroll-sebastian-vettel-aston-martin-silverstone-british-b1883602.html |access-date=6 March 2023 |website=The Independent |language=en |archive-date=6 March 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230306033840/https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/lawrence-stroll-sebastian-vettel-aston-martin-silverstone-british-b1883602.html |url-status=live }}</ref> He is of [[Russian Jewish]] descent from his father's side.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Jewish driver set for F1 debut |url=http://ajn.timesofisrael.com/jewish-driver-set-f1-debut/ |access-date=31 December 2020 |website=ajn.timesofisrael.com |language=en-US |archive-date=31 October 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201031053059/https://ajn.timesofisrael.com/jewish-driver-set-f1-debut/ |url-status=live }}</ref>{{Failed verification|date=December 2025}}  Stroll races under the Canadian flag and holds both Canadian and Belgian citizenship.<ref name="motorsport-total.com-belgian">{{Cite news|url=http://www.motorsport-total.com/f1/news/2017/08/halbes-heimrennen-lance-stroll-hat-belgischen-reisepass-17082417.html|title=Halbes Heimrennen: Lance Stroll hat belgischen Reisepass|work=Motorsport-Total.com|access-date=24 August 2017|language=de|archive-date=31 December 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171231070607/http://www.motorsport-total.com/f1/news/2017/08/halbes-heimrennen-lance-stroll-hat-belgischen-reisepass-17082417.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|url=https://f1i.com/news/351865-lance-stroll-still-no-fan-of-second-home-race-at-spa.html|title=Lance Stroll still no fan of second home race at Spa|work=f1i.com|access-date=28 August 2019|language=en|archive-date=16 November 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201116223703/https://f1i.com/news/351865-lance-stroll-still-no-fan-of-second-home-race-at-spa.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He is multilingual, speaking [[English language|English]], [[French language|French]], [[Flemish dialects|Dutch]], and [[Italian language|Italian]].<ref name="Aston Martin F1">{{Cite web |last= |date=21 March 2023 |title=7 TikToks you will sacrifice sleep for from the Saudi Arabian GP |url=https://www.astonmartinf1.com/en-GB/news/feature/7-tiktoks-you-will-sacrifice-sleep-for-from-the-saudi-arabian-gp |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230323000243/https://www.astonmartinf1.com/en-GB/news/feature/7-tiktoks-you-will-sacrifice-sleep-for-from-the-saudi-arabian-gp |archive-date=23 March 2023 |access-date=23 March 2023 |website=Aston Martin F1}}</ref>

==Junior racing career==
Like many racing drivers, Stroll began his motorsport career in [[kart racing|karting]] at the age of ten.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web|url=https://www.lancestroll.com/|title=Lance Stroll – Williams Martini Racing F1 Driver|website=LanceStroll.com|access-date=9 November 2017|archive-date=26 November 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161126194840/https://www.lancestroll.com/|url-status=live}}</ref> He recorded numerous race and championship wins in his native Canada and North America and in 2008, his first year of karting, he won the Federation de Sport Automobile du Quebec rookie of the year award and driver of the year in 2009.<ref name=":0" /><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.driverdb.com/drivers/lance-stroll/|title=Lance Stroll {{!}} Racing career profile|website=driverdb.com|access-date=27 April 2017|archive-date=22 March 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190322101036/https://www.driverdb.com/drivers/lance-stroll/|url-status=live}}</ref> He was mentored by six-time World Champion {{ill|Mike Wilson (racing driver)|lt=Mike Wilson|fr|Mike Wilson (pilote)}}.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://tkart.it/en/magazine/editorial/mike-wilson-tutored-lance-stroll |url-access=subscription |title=When Mike Wilson bet on Lance Stroll |date=10 June 2019 |website=TKART |access-date=11 August 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250413141234/https://tkart.it/en/magazine/editorial/mike-wilson-tutored-lance-stroll |archive-date=13 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> In 2010, Stroll became a member of the [[Ferrari Driver Academy]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.racefans.net/lance-stroll/|title=Lance Stroll Formula 1 driver biography|website=racefans.net|access-date=5 June 2020|archive-date=20 July 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200720080421/https://www.racefans.net/lance-stroll/|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Formula 4===
Stroll's car racing debut came in the [[2014 Florida Winter Series]], a non-championship series organized by the Ferrari Driver Academy. He raced against future Formula One competitors [[Nicholas Latifi]] and [[Max Verstappen]], and took two podium finishes as well as [[pole position]] at [[Homestead–Miami Speedway]].

Stroll made his competitive car racing debut in the [[2014 Italian F4 Championship]], driving for [[Prema Powerteam]]. Despite missing the final round due to injury, Stroll emerged as series champion, taking seven race wins, thirteen podium finishes, and five pole positions.

===Formula Three===
[[File:Lance Stroll, Formel 3 2015.JPG|thumb|left|Stroll competing in Formula Three, 2015]]

====2015====
At the beginning of 2015, Stroll won the [[New Zealand]]-based [[2015 Toyota Racing Series|Toyota Racing series]], recording ten podiums – including four wins – from sixteen race starts. In the same year, he also contested the [[2015 FIA Formula 3 European Championship|FIA Formula 3 European Championship]] with Prema Powerteam, in which his father by this time had taken a stake.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web|url=https://autoweek.com/article/formula-one/report-lance-strolls-father-spent-80-million-get-son-f1-seat|title=Report: Lance Stroll's father spent $80 million to get son Williams F1 seat|website=Autoweek|date=4 November 2016|access-date=19 March 2019|archive-date=19 March 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190319213243/https://autoweek.com/article/formula-one/report-lance-strolls-father-spent-80-million-get-son-f1-seat|url-status=live}}</ref> He competed against future Formula One competitors [[Antonio Giovinazzi]], [[Charles Leclerc]], [[George Russell (racing driver)|George Russell]] and [[Alexander Albon]], winning one race at the [[Hockenheimring]] and achieving six total podium finishes in the 33-race series. He ended the season fifth in the championship. 2015 also marked Stroll's first and only appearance at the non-championship Formula Three [[2015 Macau Grand Prix|Macau Grand Prix]], in which he finished in eighth place.

On 11 November 2015, it was announced that Stroll would leave the Ferrari Driver Academy to serve as a test driver for [[Williams Grand Prix Engineering|Williams]].

====2016====
Stroll began 2016 by finishing 5th at the [[2016 24 Hours of Daytona]], driving for [[Ford Chip Ganassi Racing]] in a Ford EcoBoost Prototype. He remained with Prema Powerteam for a third consecutive year to compete in his second season of the Formula 3 European Championship. Prior to the season, his father Lawrence hired Ferrari chief track engineer [[Luca Baldisserri]] to be Stroll's race engineer.<ref>{{cite web |title=Luca Baldisserri leaves Ferrari to mentor Formula 3's Lance Stroll |url=https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/luca-baldisserri-leaves-ferrari-to-mentor-formula-3s-lance-stroll-4995244/4995244/ |access-date=13 July 2022 |publisher=Autosport}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=4 November 2016 |title=Lance Stroll's Father Reportedly Spent $80 Million to Get Him an F1 Seat |url=https://www.roadandtrack.com/motorsports/news/a31438/lance-strolls-father-reportedly-spent-80-million/ |access-date=21 December 2024 |website=Road & Track |language=en-US}}</ref> He won the first race at [[Circuit Paul Ricard]] before taking a record thirteen more race victories over the season, including five consecutive victories in the final five races. He claimed the title with four races to go and ended the season a record 187 points clear of nearest competitor [[Maximilian Günther]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://lastwordonsports.com/motorsports/2022/12/14/lance-strolls-under-appreciated-f3-title-winning-season/|title=Lance Stroll's under appreciated F3 title-winning season|first=Fatima|last=Ahmed|date=14 December 2022|access-date=28 November 2024|website=Last Word On Sports}}</ref>

Throughout the season, Stroll and his team were accused of manufacturing his title via team orders to his teammates. This was highlighted by [[George Russell (racing driver)|George Russell]] at Paul Ricard, who claimed that "it's not a fair fight" in the wake of Stroll inheriting the lead from a slowing [[Nick Cassidy]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Prema orders to help Stroll ruining European F3, Russell believes|url=https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/prema-orders-to-help-stroll-ruining-european-f3-russell-believes-4991939/4991939/|access-date=4 December 2022|website=www.autosport.com|date=2 April 2016 |language=en|archive-date=23 May 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210523174635/https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/prema-orders-to-help-stroll-ruining-european-f3-russell-believes-4991939/4991939/|url-status=live}}</ref>

==Formula One career==
===Williams (2017–2018)===
====2017====
[[File:Lance Stroll 2017 Malaysia FP2.jpg|thumb|left|Stroll driving the [[Williams FW40]] at the [[2017 Malaysian Grand Prix]]]]
Stroll drove for the [[Williams Grand Prix Engineering|Williams]] team for the [[2017 Formula One season]], partnering [[Felipe Massa]]. He became the first [[Canadian Formula One driver]] since the {{F1|1997}} World Drivers' Champion [[Jacques Villeneuve]].<ref name="Williams">{{cite web |url=http://www.williamsf1.com/racing/news/williamsconfirmsdriverlineupfor2017season |title=Williams Confirms Driver Line Up for the 2017 Season |publisher=Williams Martini Racing |date=3 November 2016 |access-date=7 December 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161103161549/http://www.williamsf1.com/racing/news/williamsconfirmsdriverlineupfor2017season |archive-date=3 November 2016 |url-status=dead }}</ref> Reportedly, Stroll's father [[Lawrence Stroll]] paid $80 million to Williams prior to his Formula One debut.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Barclay|first=Alexander|date=21 April 2019|title=Lance Stroll - All money or a truly talented driver?|url=https://drivetribe.com/p/lance-stroll-all-money-or-a-truly-FS1EfAsDTHyjkNPK_BUPKg|access-date=6 July 2021|website=DriveTribe|language=en|archive-date=16 January 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220116081539/https://drivetribe.com/p/lance-stroll-all-money-or-a-truly-FS1EfAsDTHyjkNPK_BUPKg|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref name=":1" />

Stroll crashed in practice for his debut race, the {{F1 GP|2017|Australian}}, and received a grid penalty as this necessitated an unscheduled gearbox change.<ref>{{cite web |last=Noble |first=Jonathan |url=http://www.autosport.com/news/report.php/id/128636/stroll-gets-grid-penalty-for-gearbox-change |title=Stroll hit with gearbox change grid penalty into Australian GP |work=Autosport.com |date=25 March 2017 |access-date=25 March 2017 |archive-date=2 June 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170602034808/http://www.autosport.com/news/report.php/id/128636/stroll-gets-grid-penalty-for-gearbox-change |url-status=live }}</ref> He retired from the race with a brake failure. Two more retirements followed after collisions with [[Sergio Pérez]] at the {{F1 GP|2017|Chinese}} and [[Carlos Sainz Jr.]] at the {{F1 GP|2017|Bahrain}}. Stroll's first race finish came at the {{F1 GP|2017|Russian}}, where he finished in eleventh despite spinning on the first lap.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://montrealgazette.com/sports/auto-racing/montrealer-lance-stroll-finishes-first-career-f1-race-in-russsia|title=Montrealer Lance Stroll finishes first career F1 race in Russia|date=30 April 2017|access-date=27 January 2019|archive-date=25 January 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190125141220/https://montrealgazette.com/sports/auto-racing/montrealer-lance-stroll-finishes-first-career-f1-race-in-russsia|url-status=live}}</ref> He retired with a brake failure at the {{F1 GP|2017|Monaco}}, but was still classified fifteenth. Stroll scored his first Formula One points at his [[2017 Canadian Grand Prix|home Grand Prix]] in Montreal, finishing in ninth place.

At the {{F1 GP|2017|Azerbaijan}}, Stroll had run in second place in the closing laps, but was passed by [[Valtteri Bottas]] just metres from the finish line. He finished third to become the youngest rookie and the second-youngest driver after [[Max Verstappen]] to finish on the podium in Formula One, at the age of 18 years and 239 days.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.ctvnews.ca/montreal/article/montrealer-stroll-places-third-in-azerbaidjan-grand-prix/|title=Montrealer Stroll places third in Azerbaidjan Grand Prix|date=25 June 2017|website=ctvnews.ca|access-date=1 July 2017|archive-date=28 June 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170628001009/http://montreal.ctvnews.ca/montrealer-stroll-places-third-in-azerbaidjan-grand-prix-1.3475252|url-status=live}}</ref> becoming the [[List of Formula One driver records#Youngest drivers to score a podium finish|second-youngest driver to score a podium finish]] and the youngest to do so during their rookie season.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.statsf1.com/en/statistiques/pilote/podium/age.aspx|title=Statistics Drivers – Podiums – By age|website=StatsF1.com|access-date=1 December 2018|archive-date=2 December 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181202024649/http://www.statsf1.com/en/statistiques/pilote/podium/age.aspx|url-status=live}}</ref>

Stroll registered the fourth fastest time during a wet qualifying session for the {{F1 GP|2017|Italian}}. Due to Red Bull drivers [[Daniel Ricciardo]] and [[Max Verstappen]] (respectively third and second) taking grid penalties, Stroll was promoted to second place on the starting grid, making him the youngest Formula One driver to start on the front row at the age of 18 years and 310 days.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/headlines/2017/9/stroll--i-was-just-having-fun.html|title='I was just having fun' – rookie Stroll makes Monza front row|date=2 September 2017|website=formula1.com|access-date=2 September 2017|archive-date=2 September 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170902210420/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/headlines/2017/9/stroll--i-was-just-having-fun.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Stroll finished seventh in the race. He recorded two eighth-place finishes at the [[2017 Singapore Grand Prix|Singapore]] (where he started eighteenth) and [[2017 Malaysian Grand Prix|Malaysian]] Grands Prix. At the latter, Stroll and [[Sebastian Vettel]] collided on the cool-down lap after the end of the race. Both drivers blamed the other for the incident, however no action was taken by the stewards.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.no-further-action-over-vettel-stroll-post-race-crash.4sDB7xozKguKUUgkSCqeAG.html|title=No further action over Vettel-Stroll post-race crash|website=formula1.com|date=1 October 2017|access-date=7 November 2021|archive-date=7 November 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211107145908/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.no-further-action-over-vettel-stroll-post-race-crash.4sDB7xozKguKUUgkSCqeAG.html|url-status=live}}</ref>

At the {{F1 GP|2017|Mexican}}, Stroll worked his way up to sixth place in the race from eleventh on the grid.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.thecheckeredflag.co.uk/2017/10/lance-stroll-great-result-great-birthday-present/|title=Lance Stroll: "A great result and a great birthday present"|date=30 October 2017|website=thecheckeredflag.co.uk|access-date=30 October 2017|archive-date=7 November 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171107025012/https://www.thecheckeredflag.co.uk/2017/10/lance-stroll-great-result-great-birthday-present/|url-status=live}}</ref> Stroll ended the season twelfth in the standings, one place below teammate Massa who had both outqualified and outraced Stroll 17–2 and 9–4 (in races both drivers finished) respectively.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Collantine |first=Keith |date=1 December 2017 |title=2017 F1 team mate battles: Massa vs Stroll at Williams |url=https://www.racefans.net/2017/12/01/2017-f1-team-mate-battles-massa-vs-stroll-at-williams/ |access-date=21 December 2024 |website=RaceFans |language=en-GB}}</ref> Furthermore, Stroll gained more positions on the opening lap than any other driver that year.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.espn.com/f1/story/_/id/22499721/williams-expecting-really-big-step-lance-stroll-2018|title=Williams expects 'really big step' from Stroll in 2018|website=espn.com|date=19 February 2018|access-date=28 February 2018|archive-date=28 February 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180228161806/http://www.espn.com/f1/story/_/id/22499721/williams-expecting-really-big-step-lance-stroll-2018|url-status=live}}</ref>

====2018====
[[File:FIA F1 Austria 2018 Nr. 18 Stroll.jpg|alt=|thumb|right|Stroll at the [[2018 Austrian Grand Prix]]]]
For the [[2018 Formula One Season|2018 season]], Stroll remained with Williams, partnered by [[Sergey Sirotkin (racing driver)|Sergey Sirotkin]] after Massa retired from Formula One. The [[Williams FW41]] was the slowest car of the field and the team finished last in the constructors' championship that season. Stroll scored the team's first points of the year at the {{F1 GP|2018|Azerbaijan}} by finishing eighth. Stroll's home race, the {{F1 GP|2018|Canadian}}, ended on the first lap after a heavy collision with [[Brendon Hartley]]. He then retired from the following {{F1 GP|2018|French}} with a tire puncture. His second and final retirement of the year came at the {{F1 GP|2018|German}} with a brake failure. Stroll made his only appearance in the third qualifying session (Q3) at the {{F1 GP|2018|Italian}}, qualifying tenth. He went on to finish ninth in the race with teammate Sirotkin in tenth, marking Williams' only double points-finish that season.

Stroll finished eighteenth in the Drivers' Championship, scoring six of the team's seven points. Sirotkin out-qualified Stroll at twelve of the twenty-one races.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/11558789/f1-2018-the-final-qualifying-scores|title=F1 2018: The final qualifying scores|website=skysports.com|date=24 November 2018|access-date=7 November 2021|archive-date=7 November 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211107145906/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/11558789/f1-2018-the-final-qualifying-scores|url-status=live}}</ref>

===Racing Point (2019–2020)===
====2019====
[[File:Lance Stroll during Hungarian Formula 1 GP.jpg|alt=|thumb|left|Stroll at the [[2019 Hungarian Grand Prix]]]]
Stroll switched to driving for the newly renamed [[Racing Point]] team for the {{F1|2019}} season after the team was bought by a consortium of investors led by his father Lawrence. He replaced [[Esteban Ocon]] at the team and raced alongside Sergio Pérez.<ref>{{cite news|title=Force India: Lance Stroll confirms switch from Williams|work=BBC Sport|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/46342907|access-date=30 November 2018|archive-date=8 December 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181208125100/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/46342907|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Force India F1 team finally announces Lance Stroll's 2019 deal|url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/140445/force-india-finally-announces-stroll-2019-deal|website=Autosport|date=30 November 2018 |access-date=30 September 2020|archive-date=8 November 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201108161117/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/140445/force-india-finally-announces-stroll-2019-deal|url-status=live}}</ref> Stroll scored his first points for his new team at the season-opening {{F1 GP|2019|Australian}}, finishing ninth. At the {{F1 GP|2019|Chinese}}, Stroll criticized team strategy after finishing outside of the point-scoring positions for the second consecutive race.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.planetf1.com/news/stroll-criticises-racing-points-china-strategy/|title=Stroll criticises Racing Point's China strategy|publisher=PlanetF1|date=15 April 2019|access-date=15 April 2019|archive-date=15 April 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190415132907/https://www.planetf1.com/news/stroll-criticises-racing-points-china-strategy/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.foxsports.com.au/motorsport/formula-one/f1-chinese-grand-prix-2019-live-daniel-ricciardo-renault-results-qualifying-practice-timings-timesheet-latest-news-video-highlights/news-story/3df5ef6db994dd7277f660d17299494f|title=F1 Chinese Grand Prix 2019: Daniel Ricciardo finally ends Renault qualifying hoodoo as Valtteri Bottas takes pole|last=Polychronis|first=Jacob|work=Fox Sports|date=13 April 2019|access-date=15 April 2019|archive-date=1 June 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200601104742/https://www.foxsports.com.au/motorsport/formula-one/f1-chinese-grand-prix-2019-live-daniel-ricciardo-renault-results-qualifying-practice-timings-timesheet-latest-news-video-highlights/news-story/3df5ef6db994dd7277f660d17299494f?nk=7c0f4c2b8872c7d61175c96519324086-1591008462|url-status=live}}</ref> At the {{F1 GP|2019|Spanish}} he was involved in a collision with [[Lando Norris]] that ended both drivers' races. He finished ninth at the {{F1 GP|2019|Canadian}} having started seventeenth.

In qualifying at the {{F1 GP|2019|German}}, Stroll progressed past the first qualifying session (Q1), ending a streak of fourteen Grands Prix in which he had been eliminated in Q1. He switched to slick tires late in the race as the track was drying, elevating him to second place. He missed out on a podium after being overtaken by [[Daniil Kvyat]] and Sebastian Vettel. Stroll's next points finish came at the {{F1 GP|2019|Belgian}}, where he started sixteenth and finished tenth. He scored his final points of the season after finishing ninth at the {{F1 GP|2019|Japanese}}. Stroll retired from the final two races of the season, suffering a suspension failure at the {{F1 GP|2019|Brazilian}} and brake issues at the {{F1 GP|2019|Abu Dhabi}}.

Stroll ended his first season at Racing Point fifteenth in the Drivers' Championship with 21 points, below teammate Pérez's tally of 52 points. He was out-qualified by Pérez at eighteen of the season's twenty-one races.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.racefans.net/2019-f1-season/2019-f1-statistics/2019-f1-qualifying-data/|title=2019 F1 qualifying data|website=racefans.net|access-date=5 June 2020|archive-date=1 November 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201101094609/https://www.racefans.net/2019-f1-season/2019-f1-statistics/2019-f1-qualifying-data/|url-status=live}}</ref>

====2020====
[[File:Lance Stroll, 2020 pre-season testing (4).jpg|alt=|thumb|Stroll during [[2020 Formula One pre-season testing|pre-season testing in 2020]]]]
Stroll and Pérez were retained by Racing Point for {{F1|2020}}.''<ref name="racing point 2020">{{Cite news|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/49529336|title=Racing Point: Lance Stroll and Sergio Perez confirmed for 2020 season|work=BBC Sport|date=30 August 2019|access-date=2 September 2019|archive-date=30 August 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190830162649/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/49529336|url-status=live}}</ref>'' As a result of Canada's national sporting authority resigning its mandate from the [[FIA]], Stroll raced under an American licence but was still recognised as Canadian on race weekends.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.racefans.net/2020/02/11/canadian-f1-pair-stroll-and-latifi-to-race-under-american-licenses/|title=Canadian F1 pair Stroll and Latifi to race under American licenses|date=11 February 2020|via=www.racefans.net|access-date=18 February 2020|archive-date=29 October 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211029160749/https://www.racefans.net/2020/02/11/canadian-f1-pair-stroll-and-latifi-to-race-under-american-licenses/|url-status=live}}</ref> During the {{F1 GP|2020|Austrian}}, he qualified in ninth place but later retired from the race following engine problems. His first points finish of the season came at the {{F1 GP|2020|Styrian}}. He finished seventh having overtaken [[Daniel Ricciardo]] in a move Ricciardo described as "desperate" and deserving of a penalty.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.crash.net/f1/news/939396/1/ricciardo-desperate-stroll-deserved-penalty-f1-styrian-gp-move|title=Ricciardo: "Desperate" Stroll deserved penalty for F1 Styrian GP move|website=crash.net|first=Connor|last=McDonagh|date=12 July 2020|access-date=12 July 2020|archive-date=12 July 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200712211906/https://www.crash.net/f1/news/939396/1/ricciardo-desperate-stroll-deserved-penalty-f1-styrian-gp-move|url-status=live}}</ref> Stroll qualified third and finished fourth at the {{F1 GP|2020|Hungarian}} and followed this with four more points finishes including fourth place at the {{F1 GP|2020|Spanish}}. Stroll claimed his second Formula One podium at the {{F1 GP|2020|Italian}}.<ref name="italian grand prix">{{Cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.gasly-takes-maiden-win-in-monza-thriller-from-sainz-as-penalty-leaves.2wjQyiSgOy8ggwcJlWHhsi.html|title=Gasly beats Sainz to maiden win in Monza thriller, as Hamilton recovers to P7 after penalty|date=6 September 2020|via=www.formula1.com|access-date=6 September 2020|archive-date=6 September 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200906230949/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.gasly-takes-maiden-win-in-monza-thriller-from-sainz-as-penalty-leaves.2wjQyiSgOy8ggwcJlWHhsi.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He was in second place when the race restarted after a [[Racing flags#Red flag|red flag]] period before being passed by multiple cars including [[Pierre Gasly]]. Stroll later suggested that his poor restart cost him the chance to win the race after Gasly claimed victory.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Stroll admits poor restart cost him victory chance|url=https://www.racefans.net/2020/09/06/stroll-admits-poor-restart-cost-him-victory-chance/|website=RaceFans.net|date=6 September 2020|access-date=30 September 2020|archive-date=6 September 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200906231026/https://www.racefans.net/2020/09/06/stroll-admits-poor-restart-cost-him-victory-chance/|url-status=live}}</ref> After eight races, Stroll was in fourth place in the Drivers' Championship.

A string of retirements followed beginning with the {{F1 GP|2020|Tuscan}}, where a mechanical failure caused Stroll to crash heavily, having been running in fourth place.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Stroll blames puncture or suspension failure for massive crash at Mugello|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.stroll-blames-puncture-or-suspension-failure-for-massive-crash-at-mugello.3kwEsbKeZk5SxGIbs0XZdf.html|access-date=30 September 2020|website=www.formula1.com|language=en|archive-date=28 September 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200928175856/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.stroll-blames-puncture-or-suspension-failure-for-massive-crash-at-mugello.3kwEsbKeZk5SxGIbs0XZdf.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He was eliminated from the {{F1 GP|2020|Russian}} on the first lap after contact with [[Charles Leclerc]] caused him to hit a wall. He then withdrew from the {{F1 GP|2020|Eifel}} prior to qualifying due to illness, having sat out the third practice session.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Unwell Stroll misses Nurburgring FP3, Hulkenberg on stand-by|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/stroll-nurburgring-fp3-hulkenberg-standby/4889041/?filters%5Bdriver%5D%5B0%5D%5Btitle%5D=Lance+Stroll&filters%5Bdriver%5D%5B0%5D%5Bvalue%5D=20950|access-date=10 October 2020|website=www.motorsport.com| date=10 October 2020 |language=en|archive-date=17 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201017201445/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/stroll-nurburgring-fp3-hulkenberg-standby/4889041/?filters%5Bdriver%5D%5B0%5D%5Btitle%5D=Lance+Stroll&filters%5Bdriver%5D%5B0%5D%5Bvalue%5D=20950|url-status=live}}</ref> His team confirmed he did not have [[COVID-19]], saying he had passed all necessary FIA tests in this regard.<ref>{{Cite web|date=10 October 2020|title=Stroll has flu-like symptoms but passed multiple COVID tests|url=https://the-race.com/formula-1/stroll-has-flu-like-symptoms-but-passed-multiple-covid-tests/|access-date=10 October 2020|website=The Race|language=en-GB|archive-date=16 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201016004600/https://the-race.com/formula-1/stroll-has-flu-like-symptoms-but-passed-multiple-covid-tests/|url-status=live}}</ref> He was replaced at the event by [[Nico Hülkenberg]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/hulkenberg-replaces-stroll-eifel-gp/4889188/?filters%5Bteam%5D%5B0%5D%5Btitle%5D=Racing+Point&filters%5Bteam%5D%5B0%5D%5Bvalue%5D=40090|title=F1 news: Hulkenberg replaces Stroll at Eifel GP|website=www.motorsport.com|date=10 October 2020 |access-date=10 October 2020|archive-date=24 July 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210724052618/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/hulkenberg-replaces-stroll-eifel-gp/4889188/?filters%5Bteam%5D%5B0%5D%5Btitle%5D=Racing+Point&filters%5Bteam%5D%5B0%5D%5Bvalue%5D=40090|url-status=live}}</ref> Shortly after the race, Stroll tested positive for COVID-19. He completed a 10-day isolation period and returned to racing at the {{F1 GP|2020|Portuguese}},<ref>{{Cite news|last=Benson|first=Andrew|date=21 October 2020|title=Stroll tested positive after Eifel GP|work=[[BBC Sport]]|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/54626704|access-date=21 October 2020|archive-date=21 October 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201021102405/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/54626704|url-status=live}}</ref> in which he collided with Lando Norris. This caused Stroll's eventual retirement from the race, his fourth consecutive non-finish.

Stroll took his first pole position at the {{F1 GP|2020|Turkish}} after a wet qualifying session. In doing so, he became the first [[Formula One drivers from Canada|Canadian F1 driver]] to take pole position since Jacques Villeneuve at the [[1997 European Grand Prix]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=F1: Stroll On Pole For Turkey GP, Becomes 1st Canadian Since Villeneuve To Get P1|url=https://www.carandbike.com/news/f1-stroll-on-pole-at-turkey-as-he-becomes-1st-canadian-since-villeneuve-to-get-p1-2325286|access-date=14 November 2020|website=carandbike|language=en|archive-date=14 November 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201114144748/https://www.carandbike.com/news/f1-stroll-on-pole-at-turkey-as-he-becomes-1st-canadian-since-villeneuve-to-get-p1-2325286|url-status=live}}</ref> Stroll led the race for 32 of the 58 laps, but reported severe [[Glossary of motorsport terms#G|tire graining]] and eventually fell to ninth place by the end of the race. After the race, Racing Point found damage on Stroll's front wing which they named as the cause of his tire issues.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.racefans.net/2020/11/16/racing-point-believe-front-wing-damage-caused-strolls-tyre-trouble/|title=Racing Point believe front wing damage caused Stroll's tyre trouble|website=racefans.net|first1=Dieter|last1=Rencken|first2=Keith|last2=Collantine|date=16 November 2020|access-date=16 November 2020|archive-date=16 November 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201116123138/https://www.racefans.net/2020/11/16/racing-point-believe-front-wing-damage-caused-strolls-tyre-trouble/|url-status=live}}</ref> Shortly after the {{F1 GP|2020|Bahrain}} was restarted following [[Romain Grosjean]]'s accident, Stroll's car was flipped over after making contact with [[Daniil Kvyat]] at turn eight. Stroll was uninjured and was able to extract himself from the car.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.hamilton-wins-bahrain-gp-interrupted-by-huge-grosjean-crash-as-perez-suffers.1VOaoGnobv5rik9CwmivVs.html|title=Hamilton wins Bahrain GP interrupted by huge Grosjean crash, as Perez suffers late heartbreak|website=formula1.com|date=29 November 2020|access-date=1 December 2020|archive-date=29 November 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201129173135/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.hamilton-wins-bahrain-gp-interrupted-by-huge-grosjean-crash-as-perez-suffers.1VOaoGnobv5rik9CwmivVs.html|url-status=live}}</ref> At the {{F1 GP|2020|Sakhir}}, he benefited from tire issues for the leading [[Mercedes in F1|Mercedes]] cars to finish third, earning his third podium in Formula One.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Sakhir Grand Prix: Sergio Perez claims maiden win as Mercedes error costs George Russell|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/55209835|date=12 June 2020|website=BBC Sport|language=en|access-date=12 July 2020|archive-date=6 December 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201206185845/https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/55209835|url-status=live}}</ref>

At the end of the season, Stroll stood eleventh in the Drivers' Championship, scoring 75 of the team's 210 points.{{efn|Racing Point drivers scored a total of 210 points, however the team was deducted 15 points in the Constructors' Championship due to a ruling on the legality of their car, leaving the team on 195 points. This deduction did not affect points earned in the Drivers' Championship.}}

===Aston Martin (2021–present)===
====2021====
[[File:FIA F1 Austria 2021 Nr. 18 Stroll.jpg|thumb|left|Stroll at the [[2021 Austrian Grand Prix]]]]
Stroll continued to drive for the Racing Point team in {{f1|2021}} as the team rebranded to [[Aston Martin in Formula One|Aston Martin]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Vettel has one option less: Aston Martin sticks to current drivers|url=https://www.gpblog.com/en/news/59701/vettel-has-one-option-less-aston-martin-sticks-to-current-drivers.html|date=18 May 2020|website=GP Blog|language=en|access-date=18 May 2020|archive-date=4 July 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200704183511/https://www.gpblog.com/en/news/59701/vettel-has-one-option-less-aston-martin-sticks-to-current-drivers.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He was partnered by Sebastian Vettel in place of Pérez.<ref>{{Cite news|title=Sebastian Vettel: Ferrari driver to join renamed Aston Martin team in 2021|work=BBC Sport|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/54098516|access-date=30 September 2020|archive-date=20 June 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220620180608/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/54098516|url-status=live}}</ref> Stroll qualified and finished tenth in the season-opening {{F1 GP|2021|Bahrain}}. A video of him driving over a [[curb]] at the {{F1 GP|2021|Monaco}} became a popular [[internet meme]], used as a bait-and-switch similar to [[rickrolling]], after the official broadcast interrupted a battle between Vettel, Pierre Gasly and [[Lewis Hamilton]] to show a replay of Stroll driving over the curbs.<ref>{{cite web |title=What is the Lance Stroll Interrupts Meme? |url=https://www.essentiallysports.com/f1-news-what-is-the-lance-stroll-meme/ |publisher=Essentially Sports |access-date=14 June 2021 |date=13 June 2021 |archive-date=14 June 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210614151449/https://www.essentiallysports.com/f1-news-what-is-the-lance-stroll-meme/ |url-status=live }}</ref> A high-speed tire failure at the {{F1 GP|2021|Azerbaijan}} ended Stroll's race. A similar incident then happened to Max Verstappen later in the race, prompting tire manufacturer [[Pirelli]] to conduct an investigation into the failures.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.pirelli-reveal-results-of-investigation-into-baku-tyre-failures.2pILHApKjmVjoDk8NQIvY5.html|title=Pirelli reveal results of investigation into Baku tyre failures|website=formula1.com|date=15 June 2021|access-date=7 November 2021|archive-date=7 November 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211107145906/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.pirelli-reveal-results-of-investigation-into-baku-tyre-failures.2pILHApKjmVjoDk8NQIvY5.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Stroll scored a point with tenth place at the {{F1 GP|2021|French}}, having started nineteenth after being unable to set a representative lap time in qualifying.

Stroll caused a collision on the first lap of the {{F1 GP|2021|Hungarian}} that eliminated himself and Charles Leclerc from the race and caused Daniel Ricciardo significant damage. As a result, Stroll was issued a five-place grid penalty for the next race, the {{F1 GP|2021|Belgian}}. He finished seventh at the {{F1 GP|2021|Italian}}, his best finish of the season thus far, but collided with both Vettel and Pierre Gasly at the {{F1 GP|2021|Russian}}, for which he received a ten-second penalty.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Stroll penalised for Gasly clash in Russian GP|url=https://www.msn.com/en-gb/sports/motorsports/stroll-penalised-for-gasly-clash-in-f1-russian-gp/ar-AAOQiGv?ocid=uxbndlbing |publisher=msn}}</ref> He crashed in qualifying at the {{F1 GP|2021|Mexico City}} and finished fourteenth. His best result of the season came at the {{F1 GP|2021|Qatar}} with a sixth-place finish. Stroll ended the season thirteenth in the Drivers' Championship, scoring 34 points to Vettel's 43.

====2022====
[[File:2022 British Grand Prix (52191653966).jpg|thumb|Stroll at the [[2022 British Grand Prix]]]]
Aston Martin retained Stroll and Vettel for the {{F1|2022}} season. Stroll was in eleventh place in the closing laps of the {{F1 GP|2022|Saudi Arabian}}, but lost places after a collision with [[Alex Albon]]. He failed to set a qualifying time at the {{F1 GP|2022|Australian}} due to a crash with [[Nicholas Latifi]] for which Stroll was penalised.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.must-see-stroll-and-latifi-crash-heavily-during-q1-at-albert-park.pBYksFpG7UMMIHC6y3TeD.html|title=Stroll handed three-place grid drop for Australian GP after Latifi crash in Q1|website=Formula 1|date=9 April 2022|access-date=9 April 2022|archive-date=5 May 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220505134303/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.must-see-stroll-and-latifi-crash-heavily-during-q1-at-albert-park.pBYksFpG7UMMIHC6y3TeD.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He made three pit stops during the race and later received a penalty for weaving on the straight when defending against Valtteri Bottas, finishing twelfth.<ref>{{cite news|last=Moxon|first=Daniel|date=10 April 2022|url=https://www.mirror.co.uk/sport/formula-1/breaking-australian-gp-leclerc-verstappen-26677903|title=Charles Leclerc dominates Australian GP as Max Verstappen retires again after Red Bull catches fire|newspaper=Daily Mirror|access-date=10 April 2022|archive-date=11 April 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220411085046/https://www.mirror.co.uk/sport/formula-1/breaking-australian-gp-leclerc-verstappen-26677903|url-status=live}}</ref> Stroll took his first points of the year with tenth at the [[2022 Emilia Romagna Grand Prix|Emilia Romagna Grand Prix]],<ref>{{Cite web |title=Formula 1 2022 Emilia Romagna Grand Prix results |url=https://www.racing-statistics.com/en/events/2022-emilia-romagna-grand-prix |access-date=25 July 2022 |website=Formula 1 Statistics |language=en |archive-date=5 May 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220505031503/https://www.racing-statistics.com/en/events/2022-emilia-romagna-grand-prix |url-status=live }}</ref> and followed it up with another tenth-place finish in [[2022 Miami Grand Prix|Miami]],<ref>{{Cite web |last=Andrew Lewin |date=8 May 2022 |title=2022 Miami Grand Prix - Race results from Florida |url=https://f1i.com/news/440713-2022-miami-grand-prix-race-results.html |access-date=25 July 2022 |website=F1i.com |language=en |archive-date=2 September 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220902103725/https://f1i.com/news/440713-2022-miami-grand-prix-race-results.html |url-status=live }}</ref> despite a collision with [[Kevin Magnussen]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=2022 Miami Grand Prix: Magnussen and Stroll collide in final stages |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/video.2022-miami-grand-prix-magnussen-and-stroll-collide-in-final-stages.1732295764072043306.html |access-date=25 July 2022 |website=Formula 1 |archive-date=25 July 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220725185940/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/video.2022-miami-grand-prix-magnussen-and-stroll-collide-in-final-stages.1732295764072043306.html |url-status=live }}</ref> He crashed in qualifying at the {{F1 GP|2022|Azerbaijan}} and retired from the race with mechanical issues.

More tenth-place finishes came at the [[2022 Canadian Grand Prix|Canadian]], [[2022 French Grand Prix|French]] and [[2022 Dutch Grand Prix|Dutch]] Grands Prix.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Lance Stroll points|url=https://www.statsf1.com/en/lance-stroll/point.aspx|access-date=5 September 2022|website=StatsF1|archive-date=21 October 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221021221319/https://www.statsf1.com/en/lance-stroll/point.aspx|url-status=live}}</ref> Stroll came close to points at the {{F1 GP|2022|British}}, where he started twentieth and finished eleventh, and at the {{F1 GP|2022|Hungarian}}, where he was running eighth before being spun around by Daniel Ricciardo.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Savage |first=Nic |date=1 August 2022 |title=Daniel Ricciardo penalised for collision with Lance Stroll at Hungarian Grand Prix |url=https://www.news.com.au/sport/motorsport/formula-one/daniel-ricciardo-penalised-for-collision-with-lance-stroll-at-hungarian-grand-prix/news-story/a1ab41792ffa0268fd81797210fc83f1 |access-date=31 July 2022 |website=news.com.au |archive-date=1 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220801220749/https://www.news.com.au/sport/motorsport/formula-one/daniel-ricciardo-penalised-for-collision-with-lance-stroll-at-hungarian-grand-prix/news-story/a1ab41792ffa0268fd81797210fc83f1 |url-status=live }}</ref> Stroll's best result of the season came with sixth place at the {{F1 GP|2022|Singapore}}, and he achieved his best grid position since his [[2020 Turkish Grand Prix]] pole position at the {{F1 GP|2022|United States}}, starting fifth. He ran as high as third in the opening laps but was eliminated in a high-speed collision with [[Fernando Alonso]]. A penalty for dangerous defending against teammate Vettel in the {{F1 GP|2022|São Paulo}} sprint dropped Stroll to fifteenth on the grid for the race, in which he recovered to score a point in tenth place. He scored more points at the {{F1 GP|2022|Abu Dhabi}}, starting fourteenth and finishing eighth. Stroll ended the season fifteenth in the Drivers' Championship with 18 points to Vettel's 37.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Standings |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html |access-date=25 November 2022 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en |archive-date=28 October 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141028202800/http://www.formula1.com/results/driver/2001/40.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

====2023====
[[File:FIA F1 Austria 2023 Nr. 18 (1).jpg|thumb|left|Stroll at the [[2023 Austrian Grand Prix]]]]
Stroll remained with Aston Martin for {{F1|2023}}, partnered with Fernando Alonso who replaced the retiring Vettel.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Fernando Alonso signs to Aston Martin for 2023 on multi-year contract|date=1 August 2022|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.breaking-fernando-alonso-signs-to-aston-martin-for-2023-on-multi-year.1i8QwJht5v7dBCWFCcrqml.html|access-date=21 February 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=1 August 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220801083548/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.breaking-fernando-alonso-signs-to-aston-martin-for-2023-on-multi-year.1i8QwJht5v7dBCWFCcrqml.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Stroll missed all three days of pre-season testing at [[Bahrain International Circuit]] after suffering a cycling accident while training.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Stroll to miss pre-season testing in Bahrain after training accident|date=21 February 2023|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.breaking-stroll-to-miss-pre-season-testing-in-bahrain-after-training.5LEjhsalspXJ3QpCBwbieJ.html|access-date=21 February 2023|website=[[Formula 1]]|language=en|archive-date=20 February 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230220221425/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.breaking-stroll-to-miss-pre-season-testing-in-bahrain-after-training.5LEjhsalspXJ3QpCBwbieJ.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |title=Stroll out of pre-season test after accident |language=en-GB |work=BBC Sport |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/64709945 |access-date=23 February 2023 |archive-date=23 February 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230223110906/https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/64709945 |url-status=live }}</ref> He sustained multiple injuries in the accident including fractures in both wrists and a broken toe.<ref>{{Cite web |last= |date=7 March 2023 |title=Stroll updates fans on extent of injuries in lengthy Instagram post |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.stroll-updates-fans-on-extent-of-injuries-in-lengthy-instagram-post.4LI5SC8NBlBUazzV8KTNs8.html |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230308094601/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.stroll-updates-fans-on-extent-of-injuries-in-lengthy-instagram-post.4LI5SC8NBlBUazzV8KTNs8.html |archive-date=8 March 2023 |access-date=8 March 2023 |website=Formula 1 |language=en}}</ref> Minor surgery was performed on his right wrist with metal screws being inserted.<ref>{{cite web |date=2 March 2023 |title=Stroll shares more details on injuries sustained in 'painful' training accident as he gets set for F1 return |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.stroll-shares-more-details-on-injuries-sustained-in-painful-training.3MttPWn62jgPopse7yhg8M.html |website=Formula One |access-date=3 March 2023 |archive-date=3 March 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230303223309/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.stroll-shares-more-details-on-injuries-sustained-in-painful-training.3MttPWn62jgPopse7yhg8M.html |url-status=live }}</ref> He was replaced by reserve driver [[Felipe Drugovich]] for the test, but returned for the season-opening {{F1 GP|2023|Bahrain}}.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.aston-martin-announce-substitute-for-recovering-lance-stroll-at-pre-season.gNVAZa3HgRQVtG0c8Kmcv.html|title=Aston Martin announce substitute for recovering Lance Stroll at pre-season testing|website=Formula1.com|date=21 February 2023|access-date=26 February 2023|archive-date=21 February 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230221164420/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.aston-martin-announce-substitute-for-recovering-lance-stroll-at-pre-season.gNVAZa3HgRQVtG0c8Kmcv.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://racingnews365.com/stroll-to-race-in-season-opening-bahrain-gp|title=Stroll to race in season-opening Bahrain GP|last=Murphy|first=Luke|website=RacingNews365|date=2 March 2023|access-date=3 March 2023|archive-date=3 March 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230303223306/https://racingnews365.com/stroll-to-race-in-season-opening-bahrain-gp|url-status=live}}</ref> In the second free practice session, he reported lingering pain from his wrists that forced him to adopt a relaxed style of driving; he said that while he felt "rather stiff", he "felt alright" in the car.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://racingnews365.com/stroll-resorted-to-comfortable-wheel-positions-to-protect-hands|title=Stroll resorted to 'comfortable' wheel positions to protect hands|website=RacingNews365|last=Nichol|first=Jake|date=3 March 2023|access-date=3 March 2023|archive-date=3 March 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230303223309/https://racingnews365.com/stroll-resorted-to-comfortable-wheel-positions-to-protect-hands|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.stroll-insists-hes-fit-to-race-in-bahrain-grand-prix-despite-protecting.iUvHJnq0qI7vz6WpCC4li.html|title=Stroll insists he's fit to race in Bahrain Grand Prix despite 'protecting' wrist in practice following injury|website=Formula One|date=3 March 2023|access-date=3 March 2023|archive-date=3 March 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230303223308/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.stroll-insists-hes-fit-to-race-in-bahrain-grand-prix-despite-protecting.iUvHJnq0qI7vz6WpCC4li.html|url-status=live}}</ref> Stroll qualified eighth for the race<ref name="Bahrain2023quali">{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2023/races/1141/bahrain/qualifying.html|title=Formula 1 Gulf Air Bahrain Grand Prix 2023 – Qualifying|website=Formula 1|date=4 March 2023|access-date=4 March 2023|archive-date=8 March 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230308202940/https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2023/races/1141/bahrain/qualifying.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Bahrain2023grid">{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2023/races/1141/bahrain/starting-grid.html|title=Formula 1 Gulf Air Bahrain Grand Prix 2023 – Starting Grid|website=Formula 1|date=4 March 2023|access-date=4 March 2023|archive-date=8 March 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230308203302/https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2023/races/1141/bahrain/starting-grid.html|url-status=live}}</ref> and finished sixth despite a first-lap collision with teammate Alonso.<ref name="BAH23RESULT">{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2023/races/1141/bahrain/race-result.html|title=Formula 1 Gulf Air Bahrain Grand Prix 2023 – Race Result|website=Formula 1|date=5 March 2023|access-date=5 March 2023|archive-date=8 March 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230308203407/https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2023/races/1141/bahrain/race-result.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |title=Stroll makes 'phenomenal' recovery from fractures |language=en-GB |work=BBC Sport |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/64882794 |access-date=9 March 2023 |archive-date=9 March 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230309122943/https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/64882794 |url-status=live }}</ref> He started fifth at the {{F1 GP|2023|Saudi Arabian}} but retired from the race with engine issues.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Boxall-Legge |first=Jake |date=19 March 2023 |title=F1 Saudi Arabian GP: Perez cruises to Red Bull 1-2 as penalty denies Alonso podium |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/f1-saudi-arabian-gp-perez-cruises-to-red-bull-1-2-as-penalty-denies-alonso-podium/10446042/ |access-date=20 March 2023 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |language=en |archive-date=26 March 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230326210112/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/f1-saudi-arabian-gp-perez-cruises-to-red-bull-1-2-as-penalty-denies-alonso-podium/10446042/ |url-status=live }}</ref> He finished fourth at the {{F1 GP|2023|Australian}}, his best result of the year, despite first-lap contact with Charles Leclerc and later running into the gravel at the second restart.<ref name="Sky Sports - wild finish">{{Cite web|url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/12847996/australian-gp-max-verstappen-holds-off-lewis-hamilton-for-victory-after-wild-finish-to-chaotic-race|title=Australian GP: Max Verstappen holds off Lewis Hamilton for victory after wild finish to chaotic race|website=[[Sky Sports F1]]|date=2 April 2023|access-date=2 April 2023|archive-date=9 April 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230409110829/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/12847996/australian-gp-max-verstappen-holds-off-lewis-hamilton-for-victory-after-wild-finish-to-chaotic-race|url-status=live}}</ref>

Stroll scored points in the sprint and main race at the {{F1 GP|2023|Azerbaijan}}, but failed to score at the {{F1 GP|2023|Miami}} after being eliminated in Q1. Damage from an accident caused his retirement from the following {{F1 GP|2023|Monaco}}. He scored points at the next three races, including finishing ninth from sixteenth at the start in the {{F1 GP|2023|Canadian}}, and fourth place at the {{F1 GP|2023|Austrian}} sprint. He finished eleventh at the {{F1 GP|2023|British}} but was demoted by a penalty for colliding with Pierre Gasly. He scored points at the [[2023 Hungarian Grand Prix|Hungarian]] and [[2023 Belgian Grand Prix|Belgian]] Grands Prix, despite crashing in the sprint shootout at the latter. He finished outside the top ten at the [[2023 Dutch Grand Prix|Dutch]] and [[2023 Italian Grand Prix|Italian]] Grands Prix; his practice running at [[Monza Circuit|Monza]] was curtailed by a fuel system failure and he then qualified in last place. A heavy crash in qualifying at the {{F1 GP|2023|Singapore}} caused his withdrawal from the weekend, with Aston Martin team principal [[Mike Krack]] stating that Stroll was "still feeling the after-effects" of the accident.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.astonmartinf1.com/en-GB/news/announcement/singapore-grand-prix-statement|title=Singapore Grand Prix statement|website=astonmartinf1.com|date=17 September 2023|access-date=17 September 2023|archive-date=20 September 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230920171144/https://www.astonmartinf1.com/en-GB/news/announcement/singapore-grand-prix-statement|url-status=live}}</ref>

After qualifying seventeenth at the {{F1 GP|2023|Qatar}}, 1.1 seconds behind teammate Alonso's time, Stroll appeared to push his personal trainer in frustration as he exited the vehicle.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Woodhouse |first=Jamie |date=6 October 2023 |title=Angry Lance Stroll clashes with trainer after latest Q1 exit in Qatar |url=https://www.planetf1.com/news/lance-stroll-furious-qatar-q1-exit |access-date=6 October 2023 |website=PlanetF1 |language=en |archive-date=14 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231014080604/https://www.planetf1.com/news/lance-stroll-furious-qatar-q1-exit |url-status=live }}</ref> He finished ninth in the race but was demoted outside the points positions with a track limits penalty.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2023/races/1221/qatar/race-result.html|title=Formula 1 Qatar Airways Qatar Grand Prix 2023 – Race Result|website=Formula 1|date=8 October 2023|access-date=8 October 2023|archive-date=22 October 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022132831/https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2023/races/1221/qatar/race-result.html|url-status=live}}</ref> He started from the pit lane at the {{F1 GP|2023|United States}} but recovered to finish the race ninth; he was later promoted to seventh after the disqualifications of Lewis Hamilton and Charles Leclerc and scored his first points in six races.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Hamilton and Leclerc disqualified from United States GP |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.breaking-hamilton-and-leclerc-disqualified-from-united-states-grand-prix-for.10nvuyvEPfMgoeWxWOhw0a.html |access-date=23 October 2023 |website=www.formula1.com |language=en |archive-date=26 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231026025059/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.breaking-hamilton-and-leclerc-disqualified-from-united-states-grand-prix-for.10nvuyvEPfMgoeWxWOhw0a.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Stroll started from the pit lane again at the {{F1 GP|2023|Mexico City}} and retired with damage from a collision with Valtteri Bottas. He achieved his best qualifying result since 2020 at the {{F1 GP|2023|São Paulo}} with third place, ahead of Alonso,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.stroll-targets-podium-finish-in-brazil-after-p3-in-qualifying-as-alonso.l1uMqrrEbFJzGfq1NGI5E.html|title=Stroll targets podium finish in Brazil after P3 in qualifying as Alonso insists Aston Martin 'know what they're doing'|website=formula1.com|date=3 November 2023|access-date=3 November 2023|archive-date=12 November 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231112145416/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article.stroll-targets-podium-finish-in-brazil-after-p3-in-qualifying-as-alonso.l1uMqrrEbFJzGfq1NGI5E.html|url-status=live}}</ref> and finished fifth. He gained nine places from his starting position at the {{F1 GP|2023|Las Vegas}} to again finish fifth. Stroll ended the season tenth in the Drivers' Championship, the highest ranking in his Formula One career. He scored 74 points to Alonso's 206 and was outqualified by Alonso at nineteen of the season's twenty-two races.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://racingnews365.com/how-each-f1-teammate-fared-in-the-2023-qualifying-battle|title=How each F1 team-mate fared in the 2023 qualifying battle|website=racingnews365.com|first=Rory|last=Mitchell|date=26 November 2023|access-date=26 November 2023|archive-date=31 January 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240131211042/https://racingnews365.com/how-each-f1-teammate-fared-in-the-2023-qualifying-battle|url-status=live}}</ref> Team principal Krack defended Stroll's performance relative to Alonso, stating that despite the points difference, "there [was] not a marked gap in performance" between the two and confirmed that Stroll would remain with the team alongside Alonso for {{F1|2024}}.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/aston-martin-no-doubts-about-strolls-f1-future-at-the-team/10513782/|title=Aston Martin: No doubts about Stroll's F1 future at the team|website=autosport.com|first=Adam|last=Cooper|date=31 August 2023|access-date=26 November 2023|archive-date=31 August 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230831100942/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/aston-martin-no-doubts-about-strolls-f1-future-at-the-team/10513782/|url-status=live}}</ref>

====2024====
[[File:FIA F1 Austria 2024 Nr. 18 Stroll.jpg|thumb|Stroll at the [[2024 Austrian Grand Prix]]]]

Stroll started the 2024 season with a tenth-place finish at the [[2024 Bahrain Grand Prix|Bahrain Grand Prix]]. He then qualified tenth at the [[2024 Saudi Arabian Grand Prix|Saudi Arabian Grand Prix]], but crashed out on lap 7 after hitting the wall at turn 23. He bounced back in [[2024 Australian Grand Prix|Australia]], qualifying ninth and finishing sixth. Following the weekend, it was announced that Stroll's race engineer Ben Michell would be replaced by Andrew Vizard.<ref>{{Cite web |date=21 March 2024 |title=Stroll confirms race engineer split after Australian GP |url=https://racingnews365.com/stroll-confirms-race-engineer-split-after-australian-gp |access-date=21 December 2024 |website=RacingNews365 |language=en}}</ref>

For the first sprint weekend of the season in [[2024 Chinese Grand Prix|China]], Stroll qualified 15th for the sprint and finished the shorter race 14th. He then qualified 11th for the main race, but the main race was a disaster as Stroll finished 15th after being given a 10-second penalty for crashing into the back of [[Daniel Ricciardo]] on lap 26 following a safety car restart. After the race Ricciardo was furious with Stroll saying "I watched his onboard and he's not even looking at me, he's look at the apex, I don't know why he's not looking at the car in front."<ref>{{Cite web |date=21 April 2024 |title=Ricciardo on crash: Stroll 'made my blood boil' |url=https://www.espn.com/f1/story/_/id/39986645/ricciardo-chinese-gp-crash-stroll-made-my-blood-boil |access-date=22 July 2024 |website=ESPN.com |language=en |archive-date=18 July 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240718110114/https://www.espn.com/f1/story/_/id/39986645/ricciardo-chinese-gp-crash-stroll-made-my-blood-boil |url-status=live }}</ref>

Stroll then qualified 7th for the sprint in [[2024 Miami Grand Prix|Miami]] but retired on lap 1 due to teammate Alonso sliding into him after a collision between his teammate and [[Lewis Hamilton]]. He qualified 11th for the main race but finished 17th after a penalty for leaving the track and gaining an advantage. Stroll then qualified 13th at the [[2024 Emilia Romagna Grand Prix|Emilia Romagna Grand Prix]] but finished in 9th scoring his first points since Australia.<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.reuters.com/sports/formula1/verstappen-holds-off-charging-norris-win-imola-2024-05-19/|title=Verstappen holds off charging Norris to win at Imola|date=19 May 2024|access-date=12 March 2025|work=[[Reuters]]|last=Baldwin|first=Alan|location=[[Imola]]|editor-first=Andrew|editor-last=Heavens|editor-first2=Pritha|editor-last2=Sarkar}}</ref>

Stroll then qualified 13th for the [[2024 Monaco Grand Prix|Monaco Grand Prix]] but finished 14th after throwing his chance for points away when he got a puncture after hitting the wall in the middle of the race.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Stroll: 'My race ended after the puncture' |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/video.stroll-my-race-ended-after-the-puncture.1800133571302591896.html |access-date=22 July 2024 |website=Formula 1® - The Official F1® Website |language=en}}</ref> Stroll bounced back with a seventh-place finish at his home race in [[2024 Canadian Grand Prix|Canada]],<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.coastreporter.net/national-sports/montreals-lance-stroll-finishes-seventh-in-a-race-without-error-at-canadian-gp-9053160|title=Montreal's Lance Stroll finishes seventh in a race without error at Canadian GP|date=9 June 2024|website=Coast Reporter}}</ref> and achieved further points in [[2024 British Grand Prix|Britain]]<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.silverstone.co.uk/news/2024-f1-british-grand-prix-results-hamilton-takes-record-breaking-ninth-silverstone-win|title=2024 F1 British Grand Prix results: Hamilton takes record-breaking ninth Silverstone win|website=Silverstone}}</ref> and [[2024 Hungarian Grand Prix|Hungary]]. However, this would end up being Stroll's last points result of the season, one which he finished 13th overall.<ref>{{Cite web |title=2024 F1 Drivers Standings |url=https://www.espn.com/f1/standings |access-date=21 December 2024 |website=ESPN |language=en}}</ref> Of note was an error-strewn weekend in [[2024 São Paulo Grand Prix|Brazil]], where Stroll crashed during the qualifying session, lost his car under braking on the formation lap, and beached his car in the gravel while trying to recover back to the track.<ref>{{Cite web |date=3 November 2024 |title=Lance Stroll Crashes on Formation Lap Throwing Brazilian Grand Prix into Chaos |url=https://www.si.com/fannation/racing/f1briefings/news/lance-stroll-crashes-on-formation-lap-throwing-brazilian-grand-prix-into-chaos-01jbsbavtymt |access-date=21 December 2024 |website=F1 On SI |language=en-US |archive-date=8 December 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241208125217/https://www.si.com/fannation/racing/f1briefings/news/lance-stroll-crashes-on-formation-lap-throwing-brazilian-grand-prix-into-chaos-01jbsbavtymt |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=3 November 2024 |title=Norris under investigation over Brazilian GP aborted start mess |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/lando-norris-brazilian-grand-prix-aborted-start-investigation/ |access-date=21 December 2024 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref>

==== 2025 ====
[[File:2025 Japan GP - Aston Martin - Lance Stroll - FP3.jpg|thumb|left|Stroll (pictured at the {{F1GP|2025|Japanese}}) retained his seat for {{F1|2025}}.|alt=Stroll driving the Aston Martin AMR25 at the 2025 Japanese Grand Prix]]
Stroll retained his seat in {{F1|2025}}, finishing sixth at the rain-affected {{F1GP|2025|Australian}}.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/cr421xe109qo |title=Norris beats Verstappen in dramatic Australia opener |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=16 March 2025 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=16 March 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250316070859/https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/cr421xe109qo |archive-date=16 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He then finished ninth in [[2025 Chinese Grand Prix|China]] after disqualifications for [[Charles Leclerc]], [[Lewis Hamilton]], and [[Pierre Gasly]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/leclerc-hamilton-and-gasly-disqualified-from-chinese-gp/10706422/ |title=Leclerc, Hamilton and Gasly disqualified from Chinese GP |last=Cleeren |first=Filip |date=23 March 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=23 March 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250323122436/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/leclerc-hamilton-and-gasly-disqualified-from-chinese-gp/10706422/ |archive-date=23 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He qualified and finished last at the {{F1GP|2025|Japanese}},<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/winners-losers-f1-japanese-grand-prix-2025/ |title=Winners and losers from F1's 2025 Japanese Grand Prix |last=Suttill |first=Josh |date=6 April 2025 |website=The Race |publisher=The Race Media |access-date=6 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250406175958/https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/winners-losers-f1-japanese-grand-prix-2025/ |archive-date=6 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> before finishing seventeenth in [[2025 Bahrain Grand Prix|Bahrain]] and sixteenth in [[2025 Saudi Arabian Grand Prix|Saudi Arabia]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/stroll-calls-bahrain-a-tough-weekend-for-aston-martin-as-alonso-admits-he.7zMEwFLT1hBTf0WAMdLoPd |title=Stroll calls Bahrain a 'tough weekend' for Aston Martin as Alonso admits he 'didn't have the pace' |date=15 April 2025 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=15 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250415161911/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/stroll-calls-bahrain-a-tough-weekend-for-aston-martin-as-alonso-admits-he.7zMEwFLT1hBTf0WAMdLoPd |archive-date=15 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.autoweek.com/racing/formula-1/a64533955/first-turn-decides-oscar-piastri-cruises-f1-saudi-arabian-gp-win/ |title=First Turn Decides It as Oscar Piastri Cruises to F1 Saudi Arabian GP Win |last=Horton |first=Phillip |date=20 April 2025 |magazine=[[Autoweek]] |publisher=[[Hearst Communications]] |access-date=21 April 2025 |issn=0192-9674 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250421215406/https://www.autoweek.com/racing/formula-1/a64533955/first-turn-decides-oscar-piastri-cruises-f1-saudi-arabian-gp-win/ |archive-date=21 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

After qualifying 14th in [[2025 Spanish Grand Prix|Spain]], Stroll withdrew from the Grand Prix prior to the race due to a hand injury. In an official team statement, it was announced that he had been experiencing pain in his hand and wrist for the prior six weeks, "which his medical consultant believes is in relation to the procedure he underwent in 2023".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Cleeren |first=Filip |date=31 May 2025 |title=Lance Stroll pulls out of Spanish GP due to hand injury |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/lance-stroll-pulls-out-of-spanish-gp-due-to-hand-injury/10728541/ |access-date=31 May 2025 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=31 May 2025 |title=Aston Martin announce Stroll to miss Spanish Grand Prix |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/breaking-aston-martin-announce-stroll-to-miss-spanish-grand-prix.4FI8kbD2YhaiuMDhXgW8KO |access-date=31 May 2025 |website=Formula One |language=en}}</ref>

{{Clear left|left}}

==Other racing==
Stroll competed in two editions of the [[24 Hours of Daytona]] in [[2016 24 Hours of Daytona|2016]] and [[2018 24 Hours of Daytona|2018]] with [[Chip Ganassi Racing|CGR]] and [[Jackie Chan DC Racing|Jackie Chan DC]], respectively.{{citation needed|date=December 2025}}

In April 2026, it was announced that Stroll would be taking part in the first round of the [[2026 GT World Challenge Europe Endurance Cup]] with [[Comtoyou Racing]], alongside [[Roberto Merhi]] and [[Mari Boya]].<ref>{{cite web |date=April 2, 2026 |title=New names and returning rivals: everything you need to know about GT World Challenge at Circuit Paul Ricard |url=https://www.gt-world-challenge-europe.com/news/3162/cpr-race-preview |website=[[GT World Challenge Europe]] |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260402103937/https://www.gt-world-challenge-europe.com/news/3162/cpr-race-preview |archive-date=April 2, 2026 |access-date=April 2, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |date=April 2, 2026 |last=Thukral |first=Rachit |title=Lance Stroll correrá en GT durante el parón de la F1 en abril, con Merhi y Boya |trans-title=Lance Stroll will race in GT during the F1 break in April, alongside Merhi and Boya |url=https://es.motorsport.com/f1/news/lance-stroll-gt-paron-formula1-abril-merhi-boya/10810399/ |website=Motorsport.com |language=es |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260402104228/https://es.motorsport.com/f1/news/lance-stroll-gt-paron-formula1-abril-merhi-boya/10810399/ |archive-date=April 2, 2026 |access-date=April 2, 2026}}</ref>

